packaging_vectors.json
======================

The version strings in packaging_vectors.json are ported from the test suite
of the Python "packaging" library (https://github.com/pypa/packaging),
release 26.3, file tests/test_version.py:

  ordered        <- VERSIONS (the list "must be in the correct sorting order")
  invalid        <- TestVersion.test_invalid_versions
  normalized     <- TestVersion.test_normalized_versions
  str            <- TestVersion.test_version_str_repr
  is_prerelease  <- TestVersion.test_version_is_prerelease

They were extracted mechanically (Python ast.literal_eval of the parametrize
arguments) from the packaging-26.3 sdist published on PyPI. Test cases that
only make sense in Python (non-string arguments, sys.set_int_max_str_digits,
replace(), pickling, hashing) were not ported.

To regenerate (for example for a newer packaging release), run
extract_packaging_vectors.py in this directory; its docstring has the exact
commands. It reads literals with ast.literal_eval and never runs the tests.

